      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nWhenever you call `SendEcCommandAndReadResponse`, you pass a raw `0` for the version parameter:\n\n```c\ninternal::SendEcCommandAndReadResponse(device, EC_CMD_GET_BUILD_INFO, 0, {});\ninternal::SendEcCommandAndReadResponse(device, EC_CMD_ENTER_BOOTLOADER, 0, params_span);\n\n```\n\n**Why it\u0027s magic:** EC commands frequently have multiple versions (v0, v1, v2). Passing a raw `0` makes it look like an unused or default parameter, rather than an explicit protocol version constraint. **Fix:** Define it as a constant so it reads cleanly at the call site:\n\n```c\nconstexpr uint8_t kEcCmdVersion0 \u003d 0;\n\ninternal::SendEcCommandAndReadResponse(device, EC_CMD_GET_BUILD_INFO, kEcCmdVersion0, {});\n\n```",
