      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `cli.cc`, the CLI parsing matches against raw string literals:\n\n```c\nif (cmd_str \u003d\u003d \"enter_bootloader\") return Command::kEnterBoot;\nif (cmd_str \u003d\u003d \"flash_set_protect\") return Command::kSetFlashWp;\n\n```\n\nThese exact same string literals are then hardcoded again in `cli_test.cc`:\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cstd::string_view\u003e args \u003d {\"enter_bootloader\"};\n\n```\n\n**Why it\u0027s magic:** If a command name ever changes (e.g., `\"enter_bootloader\"` becomes `\"bootloader\"`), you have to hunt down the raw strings in both the implementation and the tests. **Fix:** Define them as `constexpr std::string_view` constants in `cli.h` so the parsing, the tests, and even the help text can share a single source of truth:\n\n```c\ninline constexpr std::string_view kCmdEnterBoot \u003d \"enter_bootloader\";\ninline constexpr std::string_view kCmdEnterRom \u003d \"enter_rom\";\n// ...\n\n```",
