      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n---\n\nIn `FakeEcTransport::Recv`, you calculate an offset and apply it directly to a raw pointer to handle partial reads:\n\n```c\nsize_t to_copy \u003d std::min(data.size(), resp.size() - recv_offset_);\n\n// POINTER MATH: resp.data() + recv_offset_\nmemcpy(data.data(), resp.data() + recv_offset_, to_copy);\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** You can eliminate the pointer math by slicing a `std::span` over the response buffer. Combined with `std::ranges::copy`, this makes the operation entirely bounds-checked and pointer-free:\n\n```c\nauto unread_data \u003d std::span(resp).subspan(recv_offset_);\nsize_t to_copy \u003d std::min(data.size(), unread_data.size());\n\nstd::ranges::copy(unread_data.first(to_copy), data.begin());\n\n```",
