      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `FakeForFlashWp::Send` and `FakeForSetWp::Send`, you extract the `tag` from the incoming USB packet using a hardcoded index of `4`:\n\n```c\nif (data.size() \u003d\u003d testing::kUsbCbwSize) {\n  std::memcpy(\u0026current_cbw_tag_, \u0026data[4], sizeof(current_cbw_tag_));\n}\n\n```\n\n**Why it\u0027s magic:** `4` represents the byte offset of the `tag` field within the USB Bulk-Only Transfer CBW. If the struct alignment or definition ever changes, this test will silently read garbage data. **Fix:** Use `offsetof` to make it mathematically tied to the structure:\n\n```c\nstd::memcpy(\u0026current_cbw_tag_, \u0026data[offsetof(BulkCbWrap, tag)], sizeof(current_cbw_tag_));\n\n```",
