      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nWhen freeing the device list, you pass a raw integer to act as a boolean flag:\n\n```c\nlibusb_free_device_list(list, /*unref_devices\u003d*/1);\n\n```\n\n**Why it\u0027s magic:** While the inline comment helps human readers, Google C++ Style strongly prefers using named constants over raw boolean/integer flags in C APIs to ensure the compiler enforces intent.   \n**Fix:**\n\n```c\nconstexpr int kUnrefDevices \u003d 1;\nlibusb_free_device_list(list, kUnrefDevices);\n\n```",
