      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n---\n\n`FindFocalDevice` uses C-style output parameters (`\u0026 out_desc`, `\u0026 out_id`) to return multiple values. Modern C++ (and Google Style) strongly prefers returning structs or `std::optional` instead of mutating references.\n\nEven better, looking at `LibusbTransport::Create()`, the `libusb_device_descriptor` isn\u0027t even used after `FindFocalDevice` returns\\! **Improvement:** Remove `out_desc` entirely, and return an `std::optional` containing a custom struct:\n\n```c\nstruct FoundDevice {\n  libusb_device* handle;\n  UsbDeviceId id;\n};\n\nstd::optional\u003cFoundDevice\u003e FindFocalDevice(std::span\u003clibusb_device*\u003e devices) {\n  for (libusb_device* dev : devices) {\n    libusb_device_descriptor desc;\n    if (libusb_get_device_descriptor(dev, \u0026desc) !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) continue;\n\n    UsbDeviceId current_id{.vid \u003d desc.idVendor, .pid \u003d desc.idProduct};\n    if (GetDeviceMode(current_id).has_value()) {\n      return FoundDevice{.handle \u003d dev, .id \u003d current_id};\n    }\n    // ... log skipped devices ...\n  }\n  return std::nullopt;\n}\n\n```",
