      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nBecause `SendActionOut` wraps `BuildFtCmd` using positional arguments, calling it sometimes requires passing meaningless `0`s just to reach a later argument. For example, in `ResetMcu`:\n\n```c\nauto res \u003d SendActionOut(device, Subcmd::kSoftReset, 0, {},\n                         TransferDirection::kSendOnly, kMcuResetTimeout, 0, 0,\n                         kSoftPor);\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** By giving the fields in `CmdFormat` (in `ft_scsi.h`) default values of `0`, you can drop the `SendActionOut` helper entirely and use C++20 designated initializers directly. It makes the call sites completely self-documenting:\n\n```c\n// In ft_scsi.h\nstruct CmdFormat {\n  Opcode opcode;\n  uint32_t address \u003d 0;\n  uint32_t length \u003d 0;\n  uint32_t aux_address \u003d 0;\n  Subcmd subcmd;\n  uint8_t flags \u003d 0;\n  uint8_t reserved \u003d 0;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n// In updater.cc, the ResetMcu call becomes:\nauto res \u003d SendBulkDataOut(device, CmdFormat{\n    .opcode \u003d Opcode::kAction,\n    .subcmd \u003d Subcmd::kSoftReset,\n    .flags \u003d kSoftPor\n}, {}, TransferDirection::kSendOnly, kMcuResetTimeout);\n\n```",
