      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn the test `UpdateFw_PadsPartialPayloadsToWordBoundary`, you test the 4KB padding logic using the magic numbers `13` and `12`:\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e fw_data(kFocalConfigSize + 13, 0xAA);\n// ...\nEXPECT_EQ(payloads[0][12], 0xAA);\nEXPECT_EQ(payloads[0][13], 0xFF);\n\n```\n\n**Why it\u0027s magic:** The number `13` is an arbitrary unaligned remainder, but without a name, `12` and `13` just look like random array accesses in the assertion block. If someone changes `13` to `20` later, they will forget to update the `12` assertion, and the test will fail.\n\n**Fix:** Define the unaligned remainder as a constant inside the test, and base the assertions dynamically on that constant:\n\n```c\nconstexpr size_t kUnalignedRemainder \u003d 13;\nconstexpr uint8_t kPayloadByte \u003d 0xAA;\nconstexpr uint8_t kPaddingByte \u003d 0xFF;\n\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e fw_data(kFocalConfigSize + kUnalignedRemainder, kPayloadByte);\n// ...\nEXPECT_EQ(payloads[0][kUnalignedRemainder - 1], kPayloadByte);\nEXPECT_EQ(payloads[0][kUnalignedRemainder], kPaddingByte);\n\n```",
