      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `GetNextCdbTagThreadSafe`, the test logic attempts to verify thread safety by having two threads race to assign to `last_tag`, and then weakly checks `EXPECT_GE(last_tag.load(), 1)`. Because threads just blindly overwrite the variable, this doesn\u0027t actually prove uniqueness or thread safety.\n\n**Improvement:** You can make this test bulletproof and much simpler. If two threads pull exactly 1,000 tags each, the *next* tag pulled on the main thread must logically be 2,001.\n\n```c\nTEST_F(UsbDeviceTest, GetNextCdbTagThreadSafe) {\n  constexpr int kIterations \u003d 1000;\n\n  auto worker \u003d [this]() {\n    for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c kIterations; ++i) {\n      device_-\u003eGetNextCdbTag();\n    }\n  };\n\n  std::thread t1(worker);\n  std::thread t2(worker);\n  t1.join();\n  t2.join();\n\n  // If the atomic increment is thread-safe, 2000 pulls have happened.\n  // The next pull must equal exactly 2001.\n  EXPECT_EQ(device_-\u003eGetNextCdbTag(), (kIterations * 2) + 1);\n}\n\n```",
